\n\\nIf I play T7, the risk is someone Chiing it. If I play T8, same. But since I have T7 and T8, maybe playing one of them is okay.\\n\\nBut why not play J2 or J3? They are honor tiles, and not part of any Chows. So playing them is safe.\\n\\nGiven that, I think playing J2 is the best option. It allows me to keep the potential for other melds and doesn't break any possible Chows.\\n\", \"output\": \"Evaluation: Playing J2 is optimal as it removes a non-meld tile, preserves potential for forming Chows in W and B suits, and avoids breaking any existing or potential melds.\\nReason: By playing J2, we maintain the possibility of forming W2-W3-W4 and B5-B6-B7 Chows, which are critical for a Pure Straight or Mixed Straight pattern. Keeping J3 intact also allows for potential Dragon Pung points if another J3 is drawn. Playing J2 minimizes the risk of breaking key melds while safely discarding an honor tile with limited strategic value.\\nAnswer: Play J2\"}"}
