ung of B6-7-8, so B7 might be more in demand. Discarding B4 would leave B5-6-7, which is a Chow. So that's a better option.\n\nSo the answer would be to play B4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard B4 to form a Chow in the B suit (B5-B6-B7), completing three Chows and a pair for the All Chows pattern.  \nReason: Discarding B4 allows the formation of B5-B6-B7 as a Chow, complementing existing Chows (W6-7-8, T7-8-9) and the W4 pair. This structure maximizes the All Chows (2 points) pattern. B4 is a safer discard than B7, as the player across has a Pung of B6-B7-B8, making B7 more likely to be needed by opponents.  \nAnswer: Play B4"}
